{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bc1DNTCujacYPJ3CKRHakH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Vendor Policy — Fictional Meridian Works (MW)\n2\t\n3\t## VEN-1 Prohibited vendors\n4\tA purchase from a prohibited vendor **must not proceed** without written compliance-officer authorization. Emergency status alone does not change this prohibition.\n5\t\n6\t## VEN-2 Exception authorization\n7\tA specific written authorization by the compliance officer permits use of an otherwise prohibited vendor for the approved transaction. No such authorization may be inferred from manager or finance approval.\n8\t\n9\t## VEN-3 Approved vendors\n10\tAn approved vendor is one designated approved in the transaction facts. The question set explicitly identifies vendor status when relevant.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0ba0ab3-d2b3-4cf0-b09d-661e49de1659","uuid":"c330d2c9-5ad4-492d-a9fc-b435778cbc76","timestamp":"2026-10-13T19:25:17.997Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\paradox-sessions-20261013\\DH_FRESH_01\\H4\\reference\\04-vendor-policy.md","content":"# Vendor Policy — Fictional Meridian Works (MW)\n\n## VEN-1 Prohibited vendors\nA purchase from a prohibited vendor **must not proceed** without written compliance-officer authorization. Emergency status alone does not change this prohibition.\n\n## VEN-2 Exception authorization\nA specific written authorization by the compliance officer permits use of an otherwise prohibited vendor for the approved transaction. No such authorization may be inferred from manager or finance approval.\n\n## VEN-3 Approved vendors\nAn approved vendor is one designated approved in the transaction facts. The question set explicitly identifies vendor status when relevant.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfznT7f9jwDRomcCQt8bT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**You need both manager approval and finance approval, and both must be in place before the purchase.**\n\n1. **Use the full total.** Thresholds are measured on the total amount including taxes and fees (EXP-4). $2,480 + $35 = **$2,515**.\n2. **The $2,500 threshold applies.** The transaction is dated October 12, 2026, which is after July 1, 2025, so the current threshold is used. The older $2,000 limit applied only before that date (AMD-1, AMD-2).\n3. **$2,515 is above $2,500,** so both approvals are needed before purchase (EXP-2, `reference/01-expense-policy.md:8`).\n\nThe subtotal alone ($2,480) is under the threshold, so it's easy to conclude that only a manager needs to approve. That's wrong: the $35 in taxes and fees pushes the total over $2,500.\n\n**Other conditions:**\n- **Vendor:** You didn't say who the vendor is. If it's on the prohibited list, you also need written authorization from the compliance officer. Manager or finance approval doesn't replace that (VEN-1, VEN-2).\n- **Emergency waiver:** The emergency rule can waive advance finance approval, but it doesn't apply here. The purchase is routine, and calling something \"urgent\" doesn't make it an emergency (DEF-1).\n- **Travel policy:** This isn't a travel purchase, so the travel rules don't apply."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":412,"cache_read_input_tokens":7557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":412},"output_tokens":474,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0ba0ab3-d2b3-4cf0-b09d-661e49de1659","uuid":"8c61e43c-1eab-48b7-8c32-0be0ac66017b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T19:25: